        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Alice Munro, Lillian Hellman\n- Works: The Moons of Jupiter, The Little Foxes\n- Roles: short story writer, Nobel Prize winner, dramatist, screenwriter, playwright\n- Organizations: Macmillan of Canada, Broadway\n\nFacts:\n- Lillian Hellman was born on June 20, 1905, and died on June 30, 1984.\n- Alice Munro was born on July 10, 1931, and her birth name was Alice Ann Laidlaw.\n- The Little Foxes is a 1939 play by Lillian Hellman and is considered a classic of 20th-century drama.\n- The Moons of Jupiter is a book of short stories by Alice Munro that was published by Macmillan of Canada in 1982.\n- Alice Munro is a Canadian short story writer and Nobel Prize winner.\n- Lillian Hellman was an American dramatist and screenwriter known for her success as a playwright on Broadway and for her left-wing sympathies and political activism.",
